            "title": "TotalEnergies Takes Contrarian Stance With $6 Billion Electricity Investment",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "TotalEnergies is making a $6 billion investment in power plants across Europe, expanding a strategy that sets it apart from rivals that seek to pump more fossil fuels.  The French oil-and-gas company said Monday it would buy 50% of a portfolio of assets owned by Energeticky a Prumyslovy Holding, the investment fund controlled by the Czech billionaire Daniel Kretinsky.  TotalEnergies is betting that investments in electricity generation\u2014a mix of renewables, gas-fired power plants and batteries\u2014can eventually match the profitability of producing fossil fuels.",
